# Code owners. A change to a path below needs a review from its owner before it
# can merge. Only two kinds of path are listed, on purpose:
#
#   the rules the project runs under: the workflows and the repository's own
#   configuration, the dependency policy, the toolchain and lint profile, the
#   workspace manifest (it holds the workspace lints and the release profile),
#   and the image and compose definitions;
#
#   the security boundary: the code that issues, checks and revokes credentials,
#   decides what a credential may do, keeps sessions with the broker, makes the
#   broker's users, and keeps the registry of principals.
#
# Everything else gets the ordinary review of any pull request. A path is added
# here when a mistake in it would change what the project allows, not because
# it is important.

# The rules
/.github/              @snowloops
/deny.toml             @snowloops
/rust-toolchain.toml   @snowloops
/clippy.toml           @snowloops
/Cargo.toml            @snowloops
/Dockerfile            @snowloops
/compose.yaml          @snowloops

# The security boundary
/crates/mansio-core/src/access.rs        @snowloops
/crates/mansio-core/src/credential.rs    @snowloops
/crates/mansio-core/src/principal.rs     @snowloops
/crates/mansio-iggy/src/access.rs        @snowloops
/crates/mansio-iggy/src/sessions.rs      @snowloops
/crates/mansio-iggy/src/provision.rs     @snowloops
/crates/mansio-server/src/auth.rs        @snowloops
/crates/mansio-server/src/credentials.rs @snowloops
/crates/mansio-server/src/registry.rs    @snowloops
/crates/mansio-server/src/records.rs     @snowloops
